# Beartropy Settings - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
This project uses **Beartropy Settings**, a database-backed settings management package for Laravel.

## API Usage

```php
use Beartropy\Settings\Facades\BeartropySettings;

# Read
BeartropySettings::get('key', 'default');
get_setting('key', 'default');

# Write
BeartropySettings::set('key', 'value');
set_setting('key', 'value');

# Check
BeartropySettings::has('key');

# All
BeartropySettings::all();
```

## Dot Notation
- `'app.name'` → group: `app`, key: `name`
- `'theme'` → group: `general`, key: `theme`

## Livewire UI
```blade
@livewire('beartropy-settings-manager')
```

## Best Practices
- Use `get_setting()` helper in Blade templates for readability
- Use `BeartropySettings` facade in PHP classes
- Group related settings with dot notation: `mail.from`, `mail.host`
- Use `config()` as fallback: `get_setting('app.name', config('app.name'))`
- Settings are cached forever — no performance concern for reads
